{"id":1752774,"retrievedAt":"2026-08-20T11:55:57.406Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":null,"belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[],"homepage":"","id":1752774,"imdb_id":null,"origin_country":["US"],"original_language":"en","original_title":"Hazardous Waste Options","overview":"This film explores the evolution of hazardous waste management in America, moving from the dangerous, unregulated dumping practices of the past to modern, sophisticated engineering solutions. It highlights the environmental risks posed by toxic industrial byproducts and details a comprehensive \"cradle-to-grave\" approach to safety. The documentary showcases various waste management technologies, including material recycling, high-temperature incineration, land treatment, and secure, clay-lined landfill cells equipped with leachate collection and groundwater monitoring systems. Ultimately, the film emphasizes the necessity of strict regulatory manifests, source reduction, and transparent community involvement to effectively manage hazardous materials while protecting public health and the environment.","popularity":0.0071,"poster_path":null,"production_companies":[{"id":308088,"logo_path":null,"name":"Stuart Finley Inc","origin_country":""}],"production_countries":[{"iso_3166_1":"US","name":"United States of America"}],"release_date":"1981-01-01","revenue":0,"runtime":22,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[],"status":"Released","tagline":"","title":"Hazardous Waste Options","video":false,"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"alternative_titles":{"titles":[]},"credits":{"cast":[],"crew":[]},"external_ids":{"imdb_id":null,"wikidata_id":null,"facebook_id":null,"instagram_id":null,"twitter_id":null},"images":{"backdrops":[],"logos":[],"posters":[]},"keywords":{"keywords":[{"id":6832,"name":"environmental protection agency"},{"id":6747,"name":"recycling"},{"id":163206,"name":"public health"},{"id":163828,"name":"landfill"},{"id":175186,"name":"hazardous waste"},{"id":175994,"name"